    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.3/p@31191",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "EMILIA.\nDoubtless\nThere is a best, and reason has no manners\nTo say it is not you. I was acquainted\nOnce with a time when I enjoyed a playfellow;\nYou were at wars when she the grave enriched,\nWho made too proud the bed, took leave o’ th’ moon\nWhich then looked pale at parting, when our count\nWas each eleven.",
